---
// src/pages/regulatory-disclosures.astro
// AMF regulatory disclosures — English version
import CompliancePage from '../layouts/CompliancePage.astro';
import { en } from '../i18n/en';
const d = en;
---

<CompliancePage
  d={d}
  lang="en"
  title="Regulatory Disclosures | Avantis Solution Financière Inc."
  description="Regulatory disclosures for Avantis Solution Financière Inc. — AMF registration, conflicts of interest, compensation disclosure and Sun Life relationship."
  heading="Regulatory Disclosures"
  updated="2025-01-01"
>

<h2>1. Regulatory Registration</h2>
<p>
  Avantis Solution Financière Inc. operates in the province of Quebec and is subject to
  regulation by the <strong>Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF)</strong>.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Firm name:</strong> Avantis Solution Financière Inc.</li>
  <li><strong>AMF registration number:</strong> [Your AMF Registration Number]</li>
  <li><strong>Category of registration:</strong> [e.g., Financial Security Advisor / Mutual Fund Dealer Representative — update to reflect your actual registration]</li>
  <li><strong>Province of registration:</strong> Quebec, Canada</li>
</ul>
<div class="info-box">
  <p>
    You can verify our registration at any time through the AMF's public register at
    <a href="https://lautorite.qc.ca/en/general-public/registers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lautorite.qc.ca</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<h2>2. Relationship with Sun Life of Canada</h2>
<p>
  Avantis Solution Financière Inc. operates within the distribution network of
  <strong>Sun Life Assurance Company of Canada</strong>. This relationship means:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>We are authorized to distribute insurance and investment products offered by Sun Life of Canada</li>
  <li>We may receive compensation (commissions, bonuses, or other remuneration) from Sun Life in connection with products we place on your behalf</li>
  <li>While we operate within the Sun Life network, our advisors act in your best interest and are not restricted to recommending only Sun Life products where alternatives may better serve your needs</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Titles and Designations</h2>
<p>
  The titles and professional designations used by our advisors reflect their specific
  qualifications and registrations. The following designations are used only by advisors
  who hold the corresponding qualification:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Financial Security Advisor (Conseiller en sécurité financière):</strong> authorized by the AMF to distribute life and health insurance products</li>
  <li><strong>Financial Planner (Planificateur financier / Pl. Fin.):</strong> this title is a protected title in Quebec, used only by holders of the Pl. Fin. designation issued by the Institut québécois de planification financière (IQPF)</li>
  <li><strong>Mutual Fund Representative:</strong> authorized to distribute mutual funds and investment products</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not use any professional title that implies qualifications or registrations we do
  not hold. If you have any questions about a specific advisor's qualifications, please
  contact us directly.
</p>

<h2>4. Compensation Disclosure</h2>
<p>
  We are committed to transparency about how we are compensated. Our advisors may receive
  compensation through the following means:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Commissions:</strong> paid by insurance companies or investment product manufacturers when products are placed on your behalf</li>
  <li><strong>Trailer fees / service fees:</strong> ongoing compensation related to investment products held in your account</li>
  <li><strong>Bonuses and incentives:</strong> from product manufacturers based on business volume, which may create a conflict of interest (see Section 5)</li>
  <li><strong>Fee-for-service:</strong> in certain cases, we may charge fees directly for financial planning services</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Specific compensation information related to products recommended to you will be disclosed
  at the point of sale, in accordance with AMF requirements.
</p>

<h2>5. Conflicts of Interest</h2>
<p>
  We are committed to identifying, disclosing and managing conflicts of interest in your
  best interest. Potential conflicts of interest include:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Product compensation:</strong> we may receive different levels of compensation for different products, which could influence recommendations — we manage this by always recommending products suited to your needs first</li>
  <li><strong>Volume incentives:</strong> some product manufacturers offer bonuses based on sales volume, which we disclose to you when relevant</li>
  <li><strong>Related party transactions:</strong> we will disclose any situation where a recommended product benefits a related party</li>
</ul>
<p>
  When a conflict of interest arises, we will inform you and obtain your consent before
  proceeding. Our advisors are required to prioritize your interests above their own
  compensation at all times.
</p>

<h2>6. Know Your Client (KYC) and Suitability</h2>
<p>
  Before making any recommendations, our advisors collect information about your financial
  situation, investment objectives, risk tolerance, and time horizon. This information is
  used to ensure that all recommendations are suitable for your specific circumstances.
  We are required by law to keep this information current and to update it whenever your
  circumstances change significantly.
</p>

<h2>7. Complaint Process</h2>
<p>
  If you have a complaint about the services or products we have provided, please follow
  this process:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Contact us directly:</strong> reach out to your advisor or our office at <a href="mailto:info@avantisfs.ca">info@avantisfs.ca</a> — we will acknowledge your complaint within 5 business days</li>
  <li><strong>Formal complaint:</strong> if your concern is not resolved to your satisfaction, you may escalate to our compliance department in writing</li>
  <li><strong>Regulatory complaint:</strong> if your complaint remains unresolved, you have the right to contact the <strong>AMF</strong> directly at <a href="https://lautorite.qc.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">lautorite.qc.ca</a> or 1-877-525-0337</li>
  <li><strong>Sun Life complaints:</strong> for complaints specifically related to Sun Life products, you may also contact <a href="https://www.sunlife.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Life of Canada</a> directly</li>
</ol>

<h2>8. Investment Product Disclosures</h2>
<p>
  For segregated fund products offered through Sun Life of Canada:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Segregated funds are subject to the terms of the variable annuity contract</li>
  <li>Unlike mutual funds, segregated funds offer maturity and death benefit guarantees on deposited capital (typically 75% or 100%)</li>
  <li>Commissions, management fees, and charges may be associated with these investments</li>
  <li>Please read the Information Folder and Contract before investing</li>
</ul>

